{"nodes": [{"id": "whitepaper_fallow", "label": "Fallow Whitepaper", "file_type": "paper", "source_file": "WHITEPAPER.md", "source_location": "line 1-29", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Evaluator-facing writeup for the Stellar frontend challenge (Level 1, White Belt): what Fallow is, why it is built this way, billing math, the custodial tradeoff, and a roadmap."}, {"id": "whitepaper_three_piece_architecture", "label": "Contributor / Registry / Consumer Architecture", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "WHITEPAPER.md", "source_location": "\u00a71 line 25-29", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Three pieces talk to one central registry; the consumer can be a person in the web UI or a headless agent hitting two HTTP endpoints."}, {"id": "whitepaper_trust_model", "label": "Container Trust Model (\u00a72)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "WHITEPAPER.md", "source_location": "\u00a72 line 33-70", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The renter never touches the host: no -v mounts, outbound-only bore relay, cap-drop ALL plus exactly seven capabilities, no-new-privileges, cgroup ceilings, and unconditional destruction on release. Explicitly out of scope: trusting the sandbox image and a kernel/Docker container escape."}, {"id": "whitepaper_capability_set", "label": "Seven Retained Linux Capabilities", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "WHITEPAPER.md", "source_location": "\u00a72 line 48-54", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "CHOWN, DAC_OVERRIDE, FOWNER, SETUID, SETGID, SYS_CHROOT, AUDIT_WRITE are the minimum for privilege-separated sshd; SYS_CHROOT is kept because without it sshd accepts the TCP connection then silently drops it before the banner."}, {"id": "whitepaper_resource_ceilings", "label": "Cgroup Resource Ceilings", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "WHITEPAPER.md", "source_location": "\u00a72 line 55-57", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "--memory-swap is pinned equal to --memory so there is no swap-based escape from the cap; limits are cgroup-enforced, not advisory."}, {"id": "whitepaper_depin_isolation_precedent", "label": "DePIN Container-Isolation Precedent", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "WHITEPAPER.md", "source_location": "\u00a72 line 62-65", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Akash, io.net, and Vast.ai all isolate at the container or VM boundary rather than the OS-permission boundary; Fallow reuses that proven model instead of inventing a new one."}, {"id": "whitepaper_billing_math", "label": "Billing Math (\u00a73)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "WHITEPAPER.md", "source_location": "\u00a73 line 74-101", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A fixed conversion chain from USD/hour to stroops/hour to a prorated per-second cost, with 1e7 stroops per XLM as Stellar's native fixed point."}, {"id": "whitepaper_usdtostroops", "label": "usdToStroops", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "WHITEPAPER.md", "source_location": "\u00a73 line 80", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "round((usd / xlmUsdPrice) * 1e7) \u2014 converts an operator-facing USD figure into Stellar's integer stroop unit."}, {"id": "whitepaper_stroopsperhour", "label": "stroopsPerHour", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "WHITEPAPER.md", "source_location": "\u00a73 line 81", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Thin wrapper over usdToStroops that fixes a node's hourly rate at rent time."}, {"id": "whitepaper_proratedcost", "label": "proratedCost", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "WHITEPAPER.md", "source_location": "\u00a73 line 82", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "round((seconds / 3600) * rateStroopsPerHour) \u2014 the single debit for a whole session, no per-minute or per-tick charge."}, {"id": "whitepaper_bill_once_design", "label": "Bill-Once-At-Release Design", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "WHITEPAPER.md", "source_location": "\u00a73 line 103-108", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Usage is already tracked continuously in memory via startedAt on the in-memory Lease, so exact duration is always available without a running total; every intermediate charge would be a Postgres write on a hot path. Collapses meter-continuously/debit-continuously into meter-continuously/debit-once \u2014 same accuracy, one write instead of N."}, {"id": "whitepaper_watchdog", "label": "Balance Watchdog and expiresAt Bound", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "WHITEPAPER.md", "source_location": "\u00a73 line 110-124", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "expiresAt = now + (balance / rateStroopsPerHour) * 3,600,000 ms answers 'how many hours does this balance afford'; a METER_INTERVAL_MS timer (default 10,000 ms) ends any lease past it, so worst-case uncollected usage is bounded by one tick rather than session length. Tightening the interval shrinks the bound at the cost of more frequent scans without touching the billing model."}, {"id": "whitepaper_debitwallet_clamp", "label": "Balance Clamped to Zero (debitWallet)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "WHITEPAPER.md", "source_location": "\u00a73 line 112-114", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Balances are clamped to zero and never go negative, which is why an unbounded overrun would become a debt the platform eats \u2014 the reason the watchdog must exist."}, {"id": "whitepaper_platform_fee_split", "label": "Platform Fee Split (PLATFORM_FEE_PCT)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "WHITEPAPER.md", "source_location": "\u00a73 line 126-135", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "fee = floor(charged * platformFeePct / 100), contributorCut = charged - fee, paid on-chain immediately so the contributor never waits on a batch payout job or a withdrawal request."}, {"id": "whitepaper_custodial_tradeoff", "label": "Custodial Tradeoff (\u00a74)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "WHITEPAPER.md", "source_location": "\u00a74 line 139-177", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Balances are an off-chain integer in Neon credited idempotently per transaction id. Non-custodial from day one would need escrow/payment channels or streaming payments, both of which turn 'watchdog checks a timestamp' into 'watchdog submits an on-chain transaction' \u2014 reintroducing the per-tick on-chain write \u00a73 exists to avoid \u2014 plus a contract-level dispute path over elapsed time. Custody is framed as a gradient of what is verifiable on-chain, not a binary."}, {"id": "whitepaper_payment_channel_escrow", "label": "Payment Channel / Escrow Alternative", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "WHITEPAPER.md", "source_location": "\u00a74 line 149-153", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Locks a renter's deposit and releases it incrementally, but needs on-chain state per active lease and a dispute path for disagreements about billed duration \u2014 beyond Level 1 scope."}, {"id": "whitepaper_streaming_payments_alternative", "label": "Streaming Payments Alternative", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "WHITEPAPER.md", "source_location": "\u00a74 line 153-156", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Stellar has no native payment streaming, so this would mean a custom Soroban contract tracking a per-second accrual rate per lease, closed out at release."}, {"id": "whitepaper_platform_private_key_exposure", "label": "PLATFORM_PRIVATE_KEY Exposure", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "WHITEPAPER.md", "source_location": "\u00a74 line 174-177", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "One key custodies every renter's prepaid balance and signs every contributor payout \u2014 the single highest-value secret in the system, called out explicitly in the deployment docs rather than softened."}, {"id": "whitepaper_ledger_contract", "label": "Soroban Ledger Contract (\u00a75)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "WHITEPAPER.md", "source_location": "\u00a75 line 181-200", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Holds no balance at any point \u2014 every call is a same-transaction relay between two existing accounts via TokenClient::transfer on the native Stellar Asset Contract. Its value over a classic payment is that each top-up and payout becomes a distinctly-typed, argument-carrying, publicly queryable event, so an outsider can identify Fallow transfers and the lease each payout belongs to without trusting Fallow's database."}, {"id": "whitepaper_contract_constructor", "label": "__constructor(platform)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "WHITEPAPER.md", "source_location": "\u00a75 line 189", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Stores the custodial address atomically at deploy \u2014 the contract's only storage."}, {"id": "whitepaper_contract_topup", "label": "topup(from, amount)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "WHITEPAPER.md", "source_location": "\u00a75 line 190", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Calls from.require_auth() so only the renter's own wallet can move their funds, relays native XLM to the platform address, and emits a public topup event."}, {"id": "whitepaper_contract_payout", "label": "payout(lease_id, contributor, user, amount)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "WHITEPAPER.md", "source_location": "\u00a75 line 191", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Requires the platform's auth, relays to the contributor, and emits an event carrying lease_id and user so each payout is attributable to a specific lease on-chain."}, {"id": "whitepaper_contract_get_platform", "label": "get_platform()", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "WHITEPAPER.md", "source_location": "\u00a75 line 192", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Read-only and callable by anyone, so the custodial address in force is publicly verifiable."}, {"id": "whitepaper_withdraw_path", "label": "Renter Withdrawal Path (withdraw)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "WHITEPAPER.md", "source_location": "\u00a74 line 166-172, \u00a76 line 210-211", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The largest single trust improvement available without a redesign, but it needs the registry to attest to a renter's off-chain balance in a way the contract can verify without simply trusting the registry's signature \u2014 likely a signed balance attestation with a nonce/expiry. Proposed, not built."}, {"id": "whitepaper_live_price_feed", "label": "Live XLM/USD Price Feed", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "WHITEPAPER.md", "source_location": "\u00a76 line 212-214", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Replace the static XLM_USD_PRICE with a Soroban oracle read or a signed off-chain feed so pricing tracks the market instead of a config value an operator must remember to update."}, {"id": "whitepaper_static_xlm_usd_price", "label": "Static XLM_USD_PRICE", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "WHITEPAPER.md", "source_location": "\u00a73 line 85-87, \u00a77 line 238", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A registry env var defaulting to 0.11 \u2014 a known limitation stated plainly rather than a live price feed."}, {"id": "whitepaper_registry_high_availability", "label": "Registry High Availability", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "WHITEPAPER.md", "source_location": "\u00a76 line 215-218", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Externalizing in-memory node/lease state (Socket.IO Redis adapter plus a shared lease store) would remove the single-instance ceiling without touching the billing model."}, {"id": "whitepaper_key_based_ssh", "label": "Key-Based SSH Upgrade", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "WHITEPAPER.md", "source_location": "\u00a76 line 219-221", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "An ephemeral keypair injected per lease is a bounded, well-understood replacement for today's wallet-address password."}, {"id": "whitepaper_mainnet_move", "label": "Mainnet Migration", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "WHITEPAPER.md", "source_location": "\u00a76 line 224-227", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Requires re-auditing custodial key handling, the contract's network-specific native-SAC constant, and fee economics against real XLM prices."}, {"id": "whitepaper_reputation_scoring", "label": "Contributor Reputation / Uptime Scoring", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "WHITEPAPER.md", "source_location": "\u00a76 line 228-229", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A natural extension of the live leaderboard's 'time served' and 'times served' metrics, but only meaningful once there is enough lease history."}, {"id": "whitepaper_streaming_settlement", "label": "Streaming Settlement (Roadmap)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "WHITEPAPER.md", "source_location": "\u00a76 line 230-231", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Evaluated only after the withdrawal path ships, not before \u2014 deliberately sequenced behind the cheaper trust improvement."}, {"id": "whitepaper_known_limitations", "label": "Known Limitations (\u00a77)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "WHITEPAPER.md", "source_location": "\u00a77 line 235-246", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every limitation is also called out at the point in the codebase it applies (db.ts, config.ts, DEPLOY.md) so the evaluator-facing document says the same thing the code comments say; the public bore.pub relay is best-effort and production should self-host bore server."}], "edges": [{"source": "whitepaper_fallow", "target": "readme_fallow", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "WHITEPAPER.md", "source_location": "line 9-10", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "whitepaper_fallow", "target": "whitepaper_three_piece_architecture", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "WHITEPAPER.md", "source_location": "\u00a71 line 25-29", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "whitepaper_three_piece_architecture", "target": "whitepaper_ledger_contract", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "WHITEPAPER.md", "source_location": "\u00a71 line 28-29", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "whitepaper_trust_model", "target": "whitepaper_capability_set", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "WHITEPAPER.md", "source_location": "\u00a72 line 48-54", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "whitepaper_trust_model", "target": "whitepaper_resource_ceilings", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "WHITEPAPER.md", "source_location": "\u00a72 line 55-57", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "whitepaper_depin_isolation_precedent", "target": "whitepaper_trust_model", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "WHITEPAPER.md", "source_location": "\u00a72 line 62-65", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "whitepaper_billing_math", "target": "whitepaper_usdtostroops", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "WHITEPAPER.md", "source_location": "\u00a73 line 79-83", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "whitepaper_stroopsperhour", "target": "whitepaper_usdtostroops", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "WHITEPAPER.md", "source_location": "\u00a73 line 81", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "whitepaper_proratedcost", "target": "whitepaper_stroopsperhour", "relation": "shares_data_with", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "WHITEPAPER.md", "source_location": "\u00a73 line 82", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "whitepaper_usdtostroops", "target": "whitepaper_static_xlm_usd_price", "relation": "shares_data_with", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "WHITEPAPER.md", "source_location": "\u00a73 line 85-87", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "whitepaper_bill_once_design", "target": "whitepaper_proratedcost", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "WHITEPAPER.md", "source_location": "\u00a73 line 103-108", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "whitepaper_watchdog", "target": "whitepaper_bill_once_design", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "WHITEPAPER.md", "source_location": "\u00a73 line 110-124", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "whitepaper_watchdog", "target": "whitepaper_debitwallet_clamp", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "WHITEPAPER.md", "source_location": "\u00a73 line 110-114", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "whitepaper_watchdog", "target": "whitepaper_stroopsperhour", "relation": "shares_data_with", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "WHITEPAPER.md", "source_location": "\u00a73 line 116", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "whitepaper_platform_fee_split", "target": "whitepaper_contract_payout", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "WHITEPAPER.md", "source_location": "\u00a73 line 134-135", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "whitepaper_platform_fee_split", "target": "whitepaper_proratedcost", "relation": "shares_data_with", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "WHITEPAPER.md", "source_location": "\u00a73 line 126-132", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "whitepaper_custodial_tradeoff", "target": "whitepaper_payment_channel_escrow", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "WHITEPAPER.md", "source_location": "\u00a74 line 149-153", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "whitepaper_custodial_tradeoff", "target": "whitepaper_streaming_payments_alternative", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "WHITEPAPER.md", "source_location": "\u00a74 line 153-156", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "whitepaper_bill_once_design", "target": "whitepaper_custodial_tradeoff", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "WHITEPAPER.md", "source_location": "\u00a74 line 156-158", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "whitepaper_custodial_tradeoff", "target": "whitepaper_ledger_contract", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "WHITEPAPER.md", "source_location": "\u00a74 line 160-166", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "whitepaper_custodial_tradeoff", "target": "whitepaper_withdraw_p